{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Etx7JPsTUN8gZrHrudQCzj","type":"tool_result","content":"# Bug: thousands separators break parse_price\n\n`parse_price(\"1,234.50\")` raises `ValueError` (it turns the comma into a dot: \"1.234.50\").\nExpected: `1234.5`.\n\nMust keep working: `\"12.50\"`, `\"$3\"`, and European decimal comma `\"12,50\"` → `12.5`.\nA comma followed by exactly three digits and then a dot (or another comma group) is a thousands separator.\nPlease add a regression test. Do not change `total_value`'s behavior.\nISSUE.md\ninventory.py\ntests/test_inventory.py","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c8f95c6-f438-45ab-9a89-6fb71bc13985","uuid":"a64238d8-63bc-4f34-ac04-c8d3830ca838","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:59:37.106Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Bug: thousands separators break parse_price\n\n`parse_price(\"1,234.50\")` raises `ValueError` (it turns the comma into a dot: \"1.234.50\").\nExpected: `1234.5`.\n\nMust keep working: `\"12.50\"`, `\"$3\"`, and European decimal comma `\"12,50\"` → `12.5`.\nA comma followed by exactly three digits and then a dot (or another comma group) is a thousands separator.\nPlease add a regression test. Do not change `total_value`'s behavior.\nISSUE.md\ninventory.py\ntests/test_inventory.py","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
